From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:37:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't read the GEM object after dropping the import
 reference

nv_dma_release_sgt() drops the reference that nv_dma_import_sgt() took on
the imported GEM object, and then reads gem->dev->driver->fops->owner for
module_put(). If that was the last reference, nvidia-drm has already freed
the object by then (KFENCE: use-after-free read in nv_dma_release_sgt, on
an object allocated by nv_drm_gem_prime_import_sg_table). KWin 6.8.1 hits
this constantly on hybrid laptops, since it imports and releases dma-bufs
for its multi-GPU copies every frame.

Look up the owner before the put, and keep the module reference until
after it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
index 81946920..93e88eae 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-dma.c
@@ -1015,6 +1015,8 @@ void NV_API_CALL nv_dma_release_sgt
     struct drm_gem_object *gem
 )
 {
+    struct module *owner;
+
     if (gem == NULL)
     {
         return;
@@ -1023,9 +1025,14 @@ void NV_API_CALL nv_dma_release_sgt
     // Do nothing with SGT, it will be unmapped and unpinned by the exporter
     WARN_ON(sgt == NULL);
 
+    // This may drop the last reference and free the GEM object, so look up
+    // its owner first. Keep the module reference until after the put, since
+    // the put may run the owner's free callback.
+    owner = gem->dev->driver->fops->owner;
+
     nv_dma_gem_object_put_unlocked(gem);
 
-    module_put(gem->dev->driver->fops->owner);
+    module_put(owner);
 }
 
 #else
